---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "Fail-Closed Multi-Tenant Security & Tenant Isolation";
const pageDesc = "Architectural principles behind AutoTelegramForward's multi-tenant isolation, fail-closed access controls, and zero cross-tenant visibility.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Features', href: url('/features/') },
    { name: 'Multi-Tenant Security', href: url('/features/multi-tenant-security/') },
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'Backup & Clone', href: url('/features/backup-clone-migration/') }}
  next={{ title: 'Getting Started Guide', href: url('/getting-started/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
    <p>
      In multi-user or shared enterprise deployments, multiple operators manage separate channels and Telegram sessions through a single AutoTelegramForward backend instance. Maintaining impenetrable tenant isolation is non-negotiable.
    </p>

    <h2 id="fail-closed-principle">The Fail-Closed Security Guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      AutoTelegramForward enforces the fundamental security principle: <strong>Missing or ambiguous identity information MUST fail closed.</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-rose-950/40 border border-rose-800/80 not-prose my-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-rose-300 mb-2">Verified Core Implementation:</h3>
      <pre class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg text-xs font-mono text-rose-200"><code>def _owns(task, owner_user_id: Optional[str]) -> bool:
    # Missing or empty owner_user_id must FAIL CLOSED
    if not owner_user_id or not str(owner_user_id).strip():
        return False
    # Cross-tenant mismatch must FAIL CLOSED
    return str(task.user_id).strip() == str(owner_user_id).strip()</code></pre>
      <p class="text-xs text-rose-200/80 mt-2">
        If an unauthenticated request or unlinked session attempts to query, list, modify, or delete a task, access is strictly denied with zero information leakage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="isolation-boundaries">Three-Tier Isolation Boundaries</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 not-prose my-6 text-xs">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1">1. Telegram Bot Tier (pro_bot_ui.py)</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">
          The Telegram Bot UI extracts <code>event.sender_id</code> and validates tenant identity before rendering any menu. Unlinked users cannot access administrative dashboards or see tasks belonging to other users.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1">2. REST & gRPC API Tier (atf-api & atf-core)</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">
          Every internal gRPC call between the Go API Gateway (8080) and Python Core (50051) carries cryptographically signed metadata containing <code>owner_user_id</code>. Servicers reject requests lacking identity headers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-white text-sm mb-1">3. Database Repository Tier</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-400">
          SQL queries strictly append <code>WHERE user_id = :owner_user_id</code>. There are no global unscoped listing endpoints accessible to standard tenants.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="credential-masking">Zero Credential Exposure</h2>
    <p>
      Sensitive values—including Telegram <code>api_hash</code>, bot tokens, MTProto phone numbers, and session auth strings—are strictly masked in logs, API responses, and Telegram Bot dialogs with <code>[REDACTED]</code> tags.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
